{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-ba5aa2cdfb24df6e", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# SelfTTS: cross-speaker style transfer through explicit embedding disentanglement and self-refinement using self-augmentation\narXiv: 2603.22252\nAuthors: Lucas H. Ueda, João G. T. Lima, Pedro R. Corrêa, Flávio O. Simões, Mário U. Neto, Paula D. P. Costa\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A model utilizing MPCL loss to generate effective label-oriented clusters for both speaker and emotion embeddings without the need for complex batching pipelines\n  2. An explicit disentanglement framework using cosine similarity loss in conjunction with GRL to effectively remove overlapping information from embeddings, thereby enabling robust cross-speaker style transfer\n  3. The use of the model's own Voice Conversion capability for Self-Augmentation to improve the naturalness of synthesized speech\n  4. A comprehensive evaluation, including cross-corpus experiments, conducted using open datasets and publicly available code\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/控制-风格标签, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多说话人", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "85cc878b-0f12-44c5-ab29-e82510ed1122", "uuid": "3173c7d9-ba1f-42a1-8576-e54bb951e957", "timestamp": "2026-08-05T09:49:09.875Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# SelfTTS: cross-speaker style transfer through explicit embedding disentanglement and self-refinement using self-augmentation\narXiv: 2603.22252\nAuthors: Lucas H. Ueda, João G. T. Lima, Pedro R. Corrêa, Flávio O. Simões, Mário U. Neto, Paula D. P. Costa\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A model utilizing MPCL loss to generate effective label-oriented clusters for both speaker and emotion embeddings without the need for complex batching pipelines\n  2. An explicit disentanglement framework using cosine similarity loss in conjunction with GRL to effectively remove overlapping information from embeddings, thereby enabling robust cross-speaker style transfer\n  3. The use of the model's own Voice Conversion capability for Self-Augmentation to improve the naturalness of synthesized speech\n  4. A comprehensive evaluation, including cross-corpus experiments, conducted using open datasets and publicly available code\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/控制-风格标签, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多说话人", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
