tegration of thinking into the modeling process for both speech understanding and generation, bridging the gap between perception and complex cognitive tasks.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/音频标记-融合, LALM/理解型, 压缩, 压缩/量化-RVQ", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "85cc878b-0f12-44c5-ab29-e82510ed1122", "uuid": "eb3c760f-ebee-4f50-99db-1cccb31f65a4", "timestamp": "2026-08-05T09:49:10.144Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# MiMo-Audio: Audio Language Models are Few-Shot Learners\narXiv: 2512.23808\nAuthors: Xiaomi LLM-Core Team, :, Dong Zhang, Gang Wang, Jinlong Xue, Kai Fang, Liang Zhao, Rui Ma, Shuhuai Ren, Shuo Liu, Tao Guo, Weiji Zhuang, Xin Zhang, Xingchen Song, Yihan Yan, Yongzhe He, Cici, Bowen Shen, Chengxuan Zhu, Chong Ma, Chun Chen, Heyu Chen, Jiawei Li, Lei Li, Menghang Zhu, Peidian Li, Qiying Wang, Sirui Deng, Weimin Xiong, Wenshan Huang, Wenyu Yang, Yilin Jiang, Yixin Yang, Yuanyuan Tian, Yue Ma, Yue Yu, Zihan Zhang, Zihao Yue, Bangjun Xiao, Bingquan Xia, Bofei Gao, Bowen Ye, Can Cai, Chang Liu, Chenhong He, Chunan Li, Dawei Zhu, Duo Zhang, Fengyuan Shi, Guoan Wang, Hailin Zhang, Hanglong Lv, Hanyu Li, Hao Tian, Heng Qu, Hongshen Xu, Houbin Zhang, Huaqiu Liu, Jiangshan Duo, Jianguang Zuo, Jianyu Wei, Jiebao Xiao, Jinhao Dong, Jun Shi, Junhao Hu, Kainan Bao, Kang Zhou, Linghao Zhang, Meng Chen, Nuo Chen, Peng Zhang, Qianli Chen, Qiantong Wang, Rang Li, Shaohui Liu, Shengfan Wang, Shicheng Li, Shihua Yu, Shijie Cao, Shimao Chen, Shuhao Gu, Weikun Wang, Wenhan Ma, Xiangwei Deng, Xing Yong, Xing Zhang, Xu Wang, Yifan Song, Yihao Zhao, Yingbo Zhao, Yizhao Gao, Yu Cheng, Yu Tu, Yudong Wang, Zhaojun Huang, Zhengju Tang, Zhenru Lin, Zhichao Song, Zhipeng Xu, Zhixian Zheng, Zihan Jiang\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We present the first empirical evidence that scaling lossless, compression-based speech pre-training to an unprecedented 100 million hours unlocks emergent task generalization, exemplified by powerful few-shot learning abilities.\n  2. We propose the first comprehensive and replicable blueprint for generative speech pre-training, which includes a novel tokenizer, a scalable architecture, a phased training strategy, and a holistic evaluation suite.\n  3. We pioneer the integration of thinking into the modeling process for both speech understanding and generation, bridging the gap between perception and complex cognitive tasks.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/音频标记-融合, LALM/理解型, 压缩, 压缩/量化-RVQ", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-96033a8b35bb137a", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Audio-Omni: Extending Multi-modal Understanding to Versatile Audio Generation and Editing\narXiv: 2604.10708\nAuthors: Zeyue Tian, Binxin Yang, Zhaoyang Liu, Jiexuan Zhang, Ruibin Yuan, Hubery Yin, Qifeng Chen, Chen Li, Jing Lv, Wei Xue, Yike Guo\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose Audio-Omni, the first unified framework for audio understanding, generation, and editing across general sound, music, and speech, featuring a decoupled architecture that bridges a frozen MLLM with a trainable DiT via a hybrid conditioning mechanism.\n  2. We introduce AudioEdit, a large-scale, high-quality dataset comprising over one million curated instruction-guided audio editing pairs constructed through a hybrid pipeline of real-world data mining and programmatic synthesis.\n  3. Extensive experiments demonstrate that Audio-Omni outperforms prior unified models and achieves competitive or superior results compared to specialized expert models across a broad range of tasks.\n  4. Audio-Omni exhibits remarkable inherited capabilities from the frozen MLLM, such as knowledge-augmented generation and zero-shot cross-lingual control, highlighting a path toward intelligent and versatile generative audio systems.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/音频标记-融合, TTS, TTS/功能-语音编辑", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "85cc878b-0f12-44c5-ab29-e82510ed1122", "uuid": "19e257b0-886b-4a04-a028-0f344d630350", "timestamp": "2026-08-05T09:49:10.412Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Audio-Omni: Extending Multi-modal Understanding to Versatile Audio Generation and Editing\narXiv: 2604.10708\nAuthors: Zeyue Tian, Binxin Yang, Zhaoyang Liu, Jiexuan Zhang, Ruibin Yuan, Hubery Yin, Qifeng Chen, Chen Li, Jing Lv, Wei Xue, Yike Guo\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose Audio-Omni, the first unified framework for audio understanding, generation, and editing across general sound, music, and speech, featuring a decoupled architecture that bridges a frozen MLLM with a trainable DiT via a hybrid conditioning mechanism.\n  2. We introduce AudioEdit, a large-scale, high-quality dataset comprising over one million curated instruction-guided audio editing pairs constructed through a hybrid pipeline of real-world data mining and programmatic synthesis.\n  3. Extensive experiments demonstrate that Audio-Omni outperforms prior unified models and achieves competitive or superior results compared to specialized expert models across a broad range of tasks.\n  4. Audio-Omni exhibits remarkable inherited capabilities from the frozen MLLM, such as knowledge-augmented generation and zero-shot cross-lingual control, highlighting a path toward intelligent and versatile generative audio systems.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/音频标记-融合, TTS, TTS/功能-语音编辑", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
